Looking at changes within two hours before 11:30:17 (i.e., 09:30–11:30 UTC), the only one that plausibly causes workers to crash is CHG-58509 on garnet-extract at 10:36 UTC, which slashed `worker.memory_limit_mb` from 4096 to 384 — a 10x cut that would starve workers of memory and cause the "worker process ended unexpectedly" crashes seen leading to the job-rejected events.

```json
{
  "faulty_change": "CHG-58509"
}
```

